# Allowed govulncheck findings in the child binaries hack/release/stage.sh stages.
#
# stage.sh scans every staged Go child (govulncheck -mode=binary) after staging
# and before signing, and reds on any finding whose trace reaches a vulnerable
# symbol in the binary unless a line below names it. One entry per line:
#
#   <GO-id> <child> <child-version> <reason> <expiry YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# <child> is the staged name (helm without its version suffix) and
# <child-version> the pin it was built or downloaded at, so a pin bump makes the
# entry match nothing and the finding is reviewed again. The reason is required
# (at least 20 characters) and says why shipping the finding is acceptable until
# the expiry, which is at most 120 days out. An expired entry is a red. An entry
# that matches no symbol-level finding in a scan is a red too: delete it, so
# exemptions do not outlive what they excused.
#
# zot v2.1.22 links go.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.46.0 (GO-2026-6505, no fixed
# version upstream), reviewed in the k3sm#815 security review. The five
# golang.org/x/net findings of that review are fixed: kine and zot are built
# against x/net v0.60.0 (internal/childreq), and stage.sh refuses a staged
# kine or zot that links an older one.
GO-2026-6505 zot v2.1.22 go.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.46.0 otlptrace exporter endpoint URL logging, which concerns an OTLP endpoint URL k3sm never configures for zot; no fixed version upstream, accepted until one ships (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
#
# helm v4.3.0 is built against golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0, whose
# openpgp/elgamal carries GO-2026-5932 (no fixed version upstream). helm links
# x/crypto/openpgp only for chart provenance signing and verification.
GO-2026-5932 helm v4.3.0 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 helm links x/crypto/openpgp only for chart provenance signing and verification (helm package --sign, helm verify, --verify on install and pull), and k3sm's helm Jobs never pass --sign, --verify or a keyring; no fixed version upstream, accepted until one ships or helm drops the package 2027-02-20
#
# kube-apiserver, kube-scheduler and kube-controller-manager v1.37.1 are built
# against golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0, and govulncheck reports GO-2026-5932 at
# package level (every openpgp package, "/*") because the binaries are stripped
# and carry no symbol table to resolve against. The v1.37.1 source vendors no
# x/crypto/openpgp package, and no openpgp package path appears in the binaries.
GO-2026-5932 kube-apiserver v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 a package-level report from a stripped binary; the v1.37.1 source vendors no x/crypto/openpgp package and the binary names none, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
GO-2026-5932 kube-scheduler v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 a package-level report from a stripped binary; the v1.37.1 source vendors no x/crypto/openpgp package and the binary names none, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
GO-2026-5932 kube-controller-manager v1.37.1 golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0 a package-level report from a stripped binary; the v1.37.1 source vendors no x/crypto/openpgp package and the binary names none, so nothing of it is linked; no fixed version upstream 2027-02-20
